=== task: multi hard
title: Which lines are errors?
prompt: `nums` holds `[3, 1, 2]`. Choose **every** line that stops the program with an error.
* `nums[3]` :: Right. The indexes are 0 to 2, so this is `IndexError: list index out of range`.
- `nums[-3]` :: -3 counts three places back from the end, to the first item, 3. It exists.
* `nums.remove(4)` :: Right. There's no 4 to remove: `ValueError: list.remove(x): x not in list`.
- `nums.index(1)` :: 1 is in the list, at index 1, so this gives 1.
* `nums.pop(3)` :: Right. There's no index 3: `IndexError: pop index out of range`.
- `nums[1:10]` :: Slices never raise errors. This gives whatever exists from index 1 on: [1, 2].
